@startuml Product Management Flow
title Product Management with Stock Intelligence

actor Admin
participant LWC as "ProductManager"
participant Controller as "ProductController"
participant Service as "StockIntelligenceService"
participant Database as "Salesforce DB"
participant AI as "Einstein AI"

== Load Products ==
Admin -> LWC: Open Product Manager
LWC -> Controller: getProductsWithStock(searchTerm, category)
Controller -> Database: SELECT FROM Product__c WITH Stock__c > 0
Database --> Controller: Product data
Controller --> LWC: ProductWrapper[]

== Stock Intelligence Check ==
Service -> Database: SELECT Stock__c, ReorderPoint__c FROM Product__c
Database --> Service: Stock data

loop For each low stock product
    Service -> AI: Analyze stock trends + predict demand
    AI --> Service: Demand prediction
    Service -> Database: UPDATE Product__c SET StockStatus__c = 'Low'
    Service -> Admin: Send notification (if configured)
end

== Bulk Import ==
Admin -> LWC: Upload CSV file
LWC -> Controller: bulkImportProducts(csvData)
Controller -> Service: validateAndImport(csvData)

loop For each product
    Service -> Database: Check existing Product__c
    alt Product exists
        Service -> Database: UPDATE Product__c
    else New product
        Service -> Database: INSERT Product__c
    end
end

Service --> Controller: Import results
Controller --> LWC: Success/error counts
LWC --> Admin: Import complete

== Stock Alerts ==
Service -> Database: SELECT products WHERE Stock__c <= ReorderPoint__c
Database --> Service: Low stock products
Service -> Admin: Email/Slack notification
Service -> Database: Log alert in StockAlert__c
@enduml